WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.163 --> 00:00:08.549
The next morning Mrs. Mellon went upstairs to Cedric's room.

2
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:13.096
For a moment she stood looking at the sleeping child.

3
00:00:13.097 --> 00:00:20.055
"The poor boy doesn't know why his mother can't stay with him," she said to herself.

4
00:00:20.056 --> 00:00:27.192
"And he'll never know. The earl has given orders that no one should tell him."

5
00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:31.860
Mrs. Mellon went over to the window and opened the curtains.

6
00:00:31.861 --> 00:00:36.617
She thought about what the footman had said after last night's dinner.

7
00:00:36.618 --> 00:00:42.851
"Lord Fauntleroy was so polite and concerned about the earl.

8
00:00:42.852 --> 00:00:48.143
It was like the boy was dining with his best friend."

9
00:00:48.144 --> 00:00:51.944
Cedric turned over and opened his eyes.

10
00:00:51.945 --> 00:00:56.745
"Good morning, my lord," Mrs. Mellon said.

11
00:00:56.746 --> 00:01:05.570
"Good morning." Cedric rubbed his eyes and looked around. "Where am I?"

12
00:01:05.571 --> 00:01:13.324
Mrs. Mellon smiled. "In your own bedroom at Dorincourt Castle.

13
00:01:13.325 --> 00:01:19.876
You fell asleep by the fire last night, and a footman carried you upstairs.

14
00:01:19.877 --> 00:01:29.302
Are you ready to get up? By the time I help you get dressed, your breakfast will be ready."

15
00:01:29.303 --> 00:01:34.277
"Thank you, but I can get dressed myself," Cedric said.

16
00:01:34.278 --> 00:01:42.511
"My mother taught me years ago. Though I sometimes have trouble with buttons."

17
00:01:42.512 --> 00:01:47.451
Cedric was soon dressed and eating breakfast in an adjoining room.

18
00:01:47.452 --> 00:01:52.860
Once again he noticed how large the rooms in the castle were.

19
00:01:52.861 --> 00:01:58.042
"Where does that door lead to?" He pointed with his spoon.

20
00:01:58.043 --> 00:02:03.282
"To another room of yours," Mrs. Mellon said.

21
00:02:03.283 --> 00:02:09.636
"You mean I have three rooms?" Cedric put down his spoon in surprise.

22
00:02:09.637 --> 00:02:14.762
"I'm a small boy to have so many big rooms."

23
00:02:14.763 --> 00:02:21.015
"You're just feeling strange because everything is new," Mrs. Mellon said.

24
00:02:21.016 --> 00:02:25.890
"The castle is such a beautiful place once you get used to it."

25
00:02:25.891 --> 00:02:32.288
"I know it's beautiful." Cedric sighed.

26
00:02:32.289 --> 00:02:37.010
"But I'd enjoy it more if I didn't miss my mother right now.

27
00:02:37.011 --> 00:02:40.055
We always had breakfast together.

28
00:02:40.056 --> 00:02:47.518
She'd let me put the sugar in her tea and butter her toast . . ."

29
00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:51.202
Cedric sighed again at the memory.

30
00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:56.899
"You can visit her every day, and you'll have so much to tell her."

31
00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.826
Mrs. Mellon patted his shoulder reassuringly.

32
00:03:00.827 --> 00:03:04.599
"Wait until you meet all the dogs and horses."

33
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:08.338
"I love horses!" Cedric said.

34
00:03:08.339 --> 00:03:14.032
"I was very fond of Jim, the horse that pulled Mr. Hobbs' grocery wagon.

35
00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:17.317
And I'd like to learn to ride."

36
00:03:17.318 --> 00:03:21.566
"Then you'll be interested in touring the stables.

37
00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:25.362
But before that, you must look in the next room."

38
00:03:25.363 --> 00:03:29.502
"What's in there?" Cedric asked.

39
00:03:29.503 --> 00:03:38.764
"Finish your breakfast, and then we'll go together," Mrs. Mellon said. "I'm sure you'll like it."

40
00:03:38.765 --> 00:03:43.378
Now Cedric was really curious about the other room.

41
00:03:43.386 --> 00:03:46.977
He finished his breakfast in no time.

42
00:03:46.978 --> 00:03:52.455
"Are you sure you're ready?" Mrs. Mellon asked as they stood before the door.

43
00:03:52.456 --> 00:03:55.359
"Yes, yes!"

44
00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.393
When Mrs. Mellon opened the door, Cedric stood on the threshold.

45
00:04:00.394 --> 00:04:04.162
He was too surprised to enter the room.

46
00:04:04.163 --> 00:04:08.920
Like all the other rooms in the castle, this one was large.

47
00:04:08.921 --> 00:04:12.705
But the furniture was smaller and the colors were brighter.

48
00:04:12.706 --> 00:04:15.755
Books filled the shelves.

49
00:04:15.756 --> 00:04:21.173
The table and floor were covered with toys and games and puzzles.

50
00:04:21.174 --> 00:04:25.999
"This looks like a boy's room," Cedric said.

51
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.397
"There are so many toys! Who do they belong to?"

52
00:04:30.398 --> 00:04:36.638
"Go look at them," Mrs. Mellon said. "They belong to you."

53
00:04:36.639 --> 00:04:40.143
"To me? Who gave them to me?"

54
00:04:40.144 --> 00:04:43.386
He sprang into the room with a look of delight.

55
00:04:43.387 --> 00:04:48.272
"Oh, I know! It was Grandpapa!"

56
00:04:48.273 --> 00:04:57.672
"You're right. And if you're a happy boy and act like a gentleman, he'll give you whatever you want."

57
00:04:57.673 --> 00:05:00.818
It was a tremendously exciting morning.

58
00:05:00.819 --> 00:05:06.583
There were so many things to examine that Cedric darted from one to the next.

59
00:05:06.584 --> 00:05:14.323
He was especially fascinated by a miniature baseball game. At last he paused.

60
00:05:14.324 --> 00:05:21.186
"And this was done just for me?" Cedric shook his head in amazement.

61
00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:28.984
"Yes, people came all the way from London to set up these rooms," Mrs. Mellon said.

62
00:05:28.985 --> 00:05:32.023
"I think they did a good job."

63
00:05:32.024 --> 00:05:35.674
Wide-eyed, Cedric nodded in agreement.

64
00:05:35.675 --> 00:05:41.268
"Did you ever know anyone who had such a kind grandfather?"

65
00:05:41.269 --> 00:05:44.385
Mrs. Mellon wasn't sure what to say.

66
00:05:44.386 --> 00:05:49.639
Yes, the earl had filled the room with an amazing assortment of toys.

67
00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.968
But his motives were not as kind as Cedric thought.

68
00:05:53.969 --> 00:05:58.553
She remembered the earl's instructions for setting up the room.

69
00:05:58.554 --> 00:06:04.760
"Give Lord Fauntleroy anything he wants," the earl had told her.

70
00:06:04.761 --> 00:06:10.660
"Keep him amused, and he'll soon forget about his mother."

71
00:06:10.661 --> 00:06:14.752
Mrs. Mellon shuddered at the memory of the earl's heartlessness.

72
00:06:14.753 --> 00:06:18.335
It was cruel to separate the boy from his mother.

73
00:06:18.336 --> 00:06:22.150
She forced herself to smile at Cedric.

74
00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:26.954
"I'm sure his lordship will send for you later today.

75
00:06:26.955 --> 00:06:35.808
He'll want to hear how you like your rooms."

